# Curitopia

Read `AGENTS.md` and `docs/DECISIONS.md` before changing behaviour. The signed-in home is the library in `app/page.tsx`. The workspace is `components/exploration-screen.tsx`. Preserve Quickfire, Focus, the SVG question map, and the accepted visual shell.

- Quickfire capture stays uninterrupted: no required categories, coaching prompts, or dialogs between questions.
- Focus starters (Investigate, Reframe, Connect, Challenge) are optional.
- Derive node colour from the stable question id. Do not store colour, and do not pick a new colour on each render.
- Approved stack: Supabase Auth, managed Supabase PostgreSQL, and Linode at https://curitopia.com. Email and password, with email confirmation and password reset. No social login. Use the local Supabase stack only to test migrations.
- A persistent exploration requires a signed-in confirmed user. Insert it when the first question is saved. Keep empty explorations out of the library.
- Titles are at most 120 characters. Question text is at most 2,000 characters. Deletion of an exploration is permanent after explicit confirmation. A question can be hidden and restored. `is_hidden` keeps the row. Hidden questions leave the normal map, list, and visible counts. The central question and the last visible question cannot be hidden.
- Enforce ownership with row-level security. Test those policies with Supabase database tests (pgTAP via `supabase test db`). Do not describe that security as fully verified until those tests, or an equivalent two-account check, have actually passed.
- Never send question text, titles, or other session content to analytics. Leave the existing Vercel Analytics component in place until D-015 settles that choice.
- Keep the `typecheck` script. Do not set `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors`.
- Reflection of one saved exploration is implemented. It does not require completion. The owner confirms before any question text is sent to OpenAI, and the result is not stored. Do not add cross-session profiling, a concept map, or AI experiment suggestions until that task is requested. Phase 1 opens one experiment from a prioritised question. Phase 2 adds, edits, and deletes its items. Phase 3 adds one optional thumbnail on any experiment item. Item editing does not call a model. Thumbnail generation sends only the submitted prompt. The hosted experiment SQL has not been applied. The first thumbnail SQL has been applied. The SQL that allows that thumbnail on every item type has not been applied.
- A saved exploration may have one optional focus image. Generate sends only the confirmed prompt. Upload does not call OpenAI. The image is stored only after Use image. The hosted focus-image SQL has not been applied.
- The previous-explorations library is the signed-in home. Do not add rename or delete until the user asks. Database changes use a new forward-only migration through the hosted Supabase workflow. Do not recreate existing tables or edit applied migrations.
- Curitopia Stories is in the application at `/explorations/[id]/story`. Artwork is generated one slide at a time after confirmation and is not stored. Download saves one silent MP4 on the device. Do not add PDF, music, narration, or social publishing until that task is requested. D-025.
